✅ Key Steps to Modify Your Code for the AI Camera:
Install the AI Camera SDK on Raspberry Pi
Run:
sudo apt install imx500-all

Convert YOLOv8 to Sony AI camera format
Export your YOLOv8 model to ONNX:
yolo export model=best.pt format=onnx

Use Sony’s Model Compression Toolkit or RasPi_YOLO repo tools to convert ONNX to .blob (Edge AI compatible format).

Deploy model to the camera

Place your .blob file on the Pi in the expected /boot/lib/firmware/imx/ directory.

Update the pipeline configuration to use the model with the camera.

Change Your Code to Read Metadata Instead of Raw Detection

You’ll no longer use model(img) for detection. Instead:

from imx500 import Imx500Camera
camera = Imx500Camera(model='your_model.blob')
frame, metadata = camera.capture()

for detection in metadata['objects']:
    x, y, w, h = detection['bbox']
    label = detection['label']
Feed Detected ROI to Your Existing QR/Barcode Detectors
Use the bounding boxes from metadata to extract ROIs and decode them as you're doing now.
